			)
		)
		(uuid "14ee7eaa-755f-4cc5-867c-0504ed9d38de")
	)
	(text "Project Description\n\nThis is a personal project for an STM32 flight computer that \nwill be flown on a high power rocket to acheive the Level 1 high power \nrocketry certification. Further details are available in the repository:\n\nhttps://github.com/esicoe/STMRocket\n\nCapabilities\n\nThe computer is able to store flight data from its two sensors:\n	- ICM42670: 6-axis IMU with a gyroscope and accelerometer.\n	- BME280: Pressure, temperature and humidity sensor.\nData from the accelerometer & gyroscope is used to activate the pyro charge\nand release the rocket's parachute (single deploy configuration). Data is\nstored in a 4 megabyte flash memory chip and is offloaded from the computer\nusing MicroSD. \n\nDuring flight, the computer is powered by a 2S LiPO with an XT30 connector.\nProgramming interfaces are SWD & USB. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 202.692 47.752 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "2b84fb72-e457-4a65-91a7-9970bdce83ae")
	)
